<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palazzo Schifanoia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1385">1385</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Palazzo Schifanoia is a palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> built for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-este">Este family</a> from 1385 as a place of leisure. Its Hall of the Months, painted around 1470 for Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borso-deste">Borso d'Este</a> by Francesco del Cossa, Ercole de' Roberti and others, combines scenes of court life, astrological figures and classical gods. The frescoes are a major work of the Ferrarese school of painting.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palazzo-schifanoia.jpg" alt="Palazzo Schifanoia" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Warburg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FE_Schifanoia_03.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
